    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Engine implementation — the load-bearing centerpiece of the send-side consolidation; modifies `.tsx`/`.ts` in the shared library consumed by every email-send surface; architecture-level decisions (reducer state machine, imperative handle contract, mount-variant layout, single canonical recipient normalization replacing 5); blocks the wrappers (021) and the Code Page mount (041). ADR-021 (Fluent v9), ADR-028 (auth decoupling), ADR-012 (shared-lib rules), ADR-022 (React version) all bind. FULL is non-negotiable.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>All-client TypeScript in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/**`; disjoint by file and language from the concurrent W1 server (C#) track. Within W2 this is the serial root — 021/023 read the engine files — but it runs safely alongside W1/W3/W7.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-12</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the canonical `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;` engine AND its sub-components in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/`. This is THE engine that replaces the 6 ad-hoc client send-email implementations, the 5 divergent recipient normalizations, and the 3 error contracts identified in the architecture assessment. Getting this right is the spine of the entire send-side (W2/W4/W6) work.

    Authoring detail is in `reference/r3-send-side-design.md` §5 (component + wrapper design), §5.4 (props contract), §5.6 (sub-components), §5.8 (validation contract), §5.10 (mount variants). Reuse it heavily — this task is the R4 realization of R3's absorbed tasks 010–020.

    Engine requirements (FR-12):
    - 5 modes: `compose | view | reply | forward | draft`
    - 3 mounts: `inline | dialog | page` — all 15 mode×mount combinations render and behave correctly
    - Internal state via a SINGLE `useReducer` (NOT scattered `useState`); state machine in `EmailComposer.reducer.ts`
    - Imperative handle via `forwardRef` + `useImperativeHandle` exposing `validate()`, `send()`, `saveDraft()`, `getState()` — wizard hosts drive these via `composerRef`
    - React 18 only (per NFR / ADR-022 non-applicability — no PCF mounts the composer directly; the Code Page is React 18). Free use of `useId`, `useTransition`, etc.
    - **No direct `@spaarke/auth` import** (ADR-028 / shared-lib decoupling). All network I/O goes through an injected `authenticatedFetch` prop, forwarded into `sendCommunication()` (task 022).
    - **Fluent UI v9 only** (ADR-021) — `@fluentui/react-components` primitives + `makeStyles` + `tokens`; dark mode passes through the host `FluentProvider`. No hardcoded colors, no v8/v0.

    Sub-components to build (rendered by the engine — `reference/r3-send-side-design.md` §5.6):
    - `RecipientField` (To/Cc/Bcc) — accepts `;`/`,`-separated paste-from-Outlook input, resolves against the existing `searchUsersAndContacts` directory lookup, renders Fluent Tags, validates free-text email on commit. **This is the single canonical normalization that replaces the 5 existing implementations.**
    - `BodyEditor` — HTML rich-text + PlainText modes with a format toggle; sends what was authored (no conversion).
    - `AttachmentList` — one section per attachment source (`local | spe | related | wizard`); enforces caps **150 attachments / 35 MB total**, warns at 25 MB (per `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md` analog); source badge + remove per item; forward-mode selection checkboxes.
    - `SendModeRadio` — rendered only when the host leaves `sendMode` unset; "Send from Spaarke" (sharedMailbox, default) vs "Send from my mailbox" (user OBO).
    - `AssociationChips` — renders `associations[]` as read-only Fluent Tags (e.g. "Matter: Smith v. Jones").
    - `ComposerActionBar` — rendered ONLY in `dialog` + `page` mounts (returns null on `inline`; the wizard frame owns navigation); Send / Save Draft / Cancel, plus view-mode Edit/Reply/Forward/Close.

    Validation contract (§5.8): `validate(): IValidationResult` with canonical codes `TO_REQUIRED`, `TO_INVALID_EMAIL`, `TO_TOO_MANY`, `SUBJECT_REQUIRED`, `BODY_REQUIRED`, `ATTACHMENT_TOO_LARGE`, `ATTACHMENTS_TOO_MANY`, `ATTACHMENT_BLOCKED_TYPE`, `FROM_REQUIRED`, `FROM_NOT_APPROVED` — one canonical set used everywhere, never duplicated per caller.

    Error contract (§5.9): `send()` throws `SendCommunicationError` (added in task 022) on non-2xx. Import it from `communicationApi.ts`; do NOT redefine.

    Barrel: export the engine + all sub-component types from `EmailComposer/index.ts`; uncomment/add the `EmailComposer` line in the shared-lib `src/index.ts` barrel. Wrappers (task 021) and unit tests (task 023) build on top of this.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React 18 + TypeScript developer fluent in Fluent UI v9 (`makeStyles`/`tokens`/`FluentProvider`) and state-machine modeling with `useReducer` + `forwardRef` + `useImperativeHandle`. Familiar with the existing `CreateRecordWizard` imperative-handle-from-host idiom and the `searchUsersAndContacts` directory lookup in the shared lib.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `EmailComposer.tsx` + reducer + types + all six sub-components compile lint-clean and render correctly across all 15 mode×mount combinations. A single `useReducer` owns engine state. The engine `forwardRef`s `IEmailComposerHandle` (`validate`/`send`/`saveDraft`/`getState`). Recipient normalization is canonical (one implementation). Attachment caps (150 / 35 MB, warn 25 MB) enforced. Mount variants visible: `page` = full-width form chrome, `dialog` = ~600px compact, `inline` = no chrome. No `@spaarke/auth` import (grep-verified). `npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` clean in `@spaarke/ui-components`; barrel exports `EmailComposer`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Empirical Finding #1 (R4 CLAUDE.md): `EmailComposer/` is absent — build from scratch. The engine is the only React component that may know email-send mechanics; the three wrappers (task 021) are ~30–60 LOC each and only lock the `mount` prop. Callers import wrappers, not the engine (design §5.1.2).

      Imperative-handle pattern: wizard hosts hold `composerRef = useRef&lt;IEmailComposerHandle&gt;()` and call `composerRef.current.validate()` on step-change and `composerRef.current.send()` on Finish. This lets the wizard own its navigation while the composer stays chrome-agnostic. Mirror the existing `CreateRecordWizard` pattern.

      Auth decoupling (ADR-028 / shared-lib rule): the engine MUST NOT `import` from `@spaarke/auth`. `authenticatedFetch` is injected via props and forwarded to `sendCommunication()`. Task 022 provides `sendCommunication()` + `SendCommunicationError`; if 022 has not landed when this task runs, import against the interface and coordinate — but 022 is a peer W2 task with no ordering dependency on 020's engine skeleton, so prefer sequencing 022 first or defining the import boundary cleanly.

      Mount-variant styling is the demanding visual piece — the `page` variant must read as a first-class entity form (it replaces the OOB `sprk_communication` form in W4). Land it as the primary visual deliverable; `dialog` + `inline` are simpler derivatives sharing the same Fluent tokens.
    </background>
