  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent UI v9 ONLY (`@fluentui/react-components`); `makeStyles` + `tokens`; dark mode via host `FluentProvider`; no hardcoded colors; no v8/v0.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Engine + sub-components MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth`. Host injects `authenticatedFetch` via props; the engine forwards it to `sendCommunication()`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Shared-library component rules — engine lives in `@spaarke/ui-components`; no fork; export via the lib barrel; no cross-package source-path imports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React version — the composer is React 18 only; ADR-022 (PCF React 16) does NOT apply (no PCF mounts the composer directly). Do not add dual-target constraints.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">`send()` throws the typed `SendCommunicationError` on non-2xx — never returns `{success:false}` and never pushes to a `warnings[]` array.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Single-engine constraint — this is the only React component that knows email-send mechanics; wrappers are thin. (ADR-045 is the R4 Communication ADR authored in task 005; supersedes the stale R3 "ADR-033" reference in the reference doc.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">RecipientField is the SINGLE canonical recipient normalization — it replaces the 5 existing implementations. No caller-local splitting/parsing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">AttachmentList caps: 150 attachments / 35 MB total (hard); 25 MB soft warning. Matches BFF enforcement + `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md` analog.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">State is a single `useReducer` source of truth; no scattered `useState` for engine state (refs / transient UI state excepted).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`ComposerActionBar` returns null on `mount='inline'` — the wizard frame owns Send/Cancel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 (spec)">Accessibility: semantic landmarks (`role="region"`, `aria-label`) per section; a live region for validation errors; full keyboard nav; focus management on mode transitions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No BFF publish-size / CVE obligations — this is client-only TypeScript (root §10 does not apply).</constraint>
  </constraints>

