  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `reference/r3-send-side-design.md` §5 in full (props contract §5.4, sub-components §5.6, validation §5.8, mount variants §5.10). Read `communicationApi.ts` to confirm the `sendCommunication()` signature + `SendCommunicationError` shape (from task 022) and how `authenticatedFetch` is parameterized. Read `userLookup.ts` for `searchUsersAndContacts`.</step>
    <step order="2">Read ADR-021 + `fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md` for Fluent v9 `makeStyles`/`tokens`/theme conventions. Read the `CreateRecordWizard` `forwardRef`/`useImperativeHandle` exemplar for shape-mirroring.</step>
    <step order="3">Author `EmailComposer.types.ts`: `EmailComposerMode`, `EmailComposerMount`, `EmailComposerBodyFormat`, `IComposerAssociation { entityName; recordId; primaryName? }`, `IComposerAttachmentSource { kind: 'local'|'spe'|'related'|'wizard'; config? }`, `IAttachmentItem`, `IRecipient`, `IValidationResult { ok; errors: { field; code; message }[] }`, `EmailComposerState`, `EmailComposerAction` (discriminated union: `SET_FIELD`, `SET_MODE`, `ADD_ATTACHMENT`, `REMOVE_ATTACHMENT`, `TOGGLE_ATTACHMENT_SELECTED`, `SET_VALIDATION_ERRORS`, `BEGIN_SEND`, `END_SEND`, `RESET`), `IEmailComposerProps` (per §5.4), `IEmailComposerHandle { validate; send; saveDraft; getState }`.</step>
    <step order="4">Author `EmailComposer.reducer.ts`: `initialState(props)` deriving from mode/mount/initial* fields; `emailComposerReducer(state, action)` as a pure immutable switch; and the `validateState(state, { forSend })` helper implementing the canonical codes (§5.8).</step>
    <step order="5">Author the six sub-components in `subcomponents/`: `RecipientField.tsx` (canonical normalization + `searchUsersAndContacts` + Fluent Tags + a11y labels), `BodyEditor.tsx` (HTML/PlainText toggle), `AttachmentList.tsx` (caps 150/35 MB, warn 25 MB, source badges, remove, forward checkbox), `SendModeRadio.tsx`, `AssociationChips.tsx`, `ComposerActionBar.tsx` (null on inline).</step>
    <step order="6">Author `EmailComposer.tsx`: `forwardRef&lt;IEmailComposerHandle, IEmailComposerProps&gt;`, `useReducer(emailComposerReducer, props, initialState)`, `useImperativeHandle` wiring `validate`/`send`/`saveDraft`/`getState`, and mount-variant layout via three `makeStyles` objects (page/dialog/inline). Compose the sub-components into `role="region"` sections with a live region for validation errors. `send()` calls `sendCommunication(mapStateToRequest(state), { authenticatedFetch: props.authenticatedFetch, bffBaseUrl: props.bffBaseUrl })` and throws `SendCommunicationError` on failure.</step>
    <step order="7">Wire mode pre-fill logic: `view` (read-only from record), `reply` (to=original from, `Re:` subject dedup, stamp `sprk_inreplyto`), `forward` (blank to, `Fwd:` dedup, wrap body, carry attachments selected, stamp `sprk_inreplyto`), `draft` (load from record; `mapStateToDraftUpdate`). Provide `dedupSubjectPrefix`, `deriveReplyState`, `deriveForwardState`, `deriveDraftState` as pure helpers (unit-tested in task 023).</step>
    <step order="8">Author `EmailComposer/index.ts` barrel (engine + wrappers placeholder + all public types + sub-component prop types). Add `export * from './components/EmailComposer';` to shared-lib `src/index.ts`.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/` (use `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` if a fresh install is needed; do NOT use `npm ci`). Both MUST be clean. Grep-verify no `@spaarke/auth` import in `EmailComposer/**`.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: invoke `code-review` skill on the new files; invoke `adr-check` against ADR-021, ADR-028, ADR-012, ADR-019, ADR-045 + `spec.md`. Address Critical + High findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 020 ✅; confirm 021 + 041 dependencies satisfied.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute protocol: status → completed; advance to next pending W2 task; record decisions (reducer shape, mount-variant token strategy).</step>
  </steps>

